  "description": "QOSJAM crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C64 H82 Dy9 N24 O42 1+,N1 O3 1-,4(C1 H4 O1),7(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy4A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy5A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 20 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.518-5.008 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 89.08-167.90°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy9(C8H9N2O)8(μ3-OH)8(μ4-OH)2(NO3)8](NO3)·4CH3OH·7H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 8 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 μ4-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 8 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 8 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 μ4-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 8 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 1 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
